# ============================================================================
# SECURITY BEST PRACTICES
# ============================================================================

# 1. NEVER commit real tokens to version control
#    - Use .env in .gitignore
#    - Use environment variables in CI/CD
#    - Use a secrets manager in production
#
# 2. Rotate tokens regularly (every 30-90 days)
#    - Most platforms support token rotation
#    - Implement in your deployment process
#
# 3. Use the minimum required scopes
#    - Each platform lists required scopes
#    - Don't request broad permissions
#
# 4. Monitor token usage
#    - Log all API calls
#    - Alert on unusual activity
#
# 5. Revoke tokens for inactive users
#    - Implement token management UI
#    - Automatically revoke after N days of inactivity
#
# 6. Use HTTPS only
#    - All API calls must use HTTPS
#    - Store tokens in secure storage
#
# 7. Implement rate limiting
#    - Respect platform rate limits
#    - Implement request queuing
#    - Handle 429 responses gracefully

# ============================================================================
# TESTING WITH MOCK TOKENS
# ============================================================================

# For local testing, you can use test tokens (don't post to real accounts):
#
# INSTAGRAM_TOKEN=test_ig_token_12345
# TIKTOK_TOKEN=test_tiktok_token_12345
# YOUTUBE_TOKEN=test_youtube_token_12345
#
# The adapter will validate tokens during requests
# Tests using mocked fetch won't require real tokens

# ============================================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING TOKEN ERRORS
# ============================================================================

# Error: "Invalid OAuth access token"
#   - Token is expired or revoked
#   - Solution: Refresh token or re-authenticate
#
# Error: "Insufficient permissions"
#   - Token doesn't have required scopes
#   - Solution: Check scopes and re-authenticate
#
# Error: "Token not found"
#   - Environment variable not set
#   - Solution: Check .env file and process.env[key]
#
# Error: "Token too short"
#   - Pasted wrong token or token is malformed
#   - Solution: Verify token format matches platform requirements
